From 757c54cdf901d026590216752acaa58bdb0d6d0a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Yuichi Kusakabe <yuichi_kusakabe@jp.honda>
Date: Thu, 3 Sep 2026 13:46:52 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] virtio-media: put the exporter's size, not the caller's, on
 the DMABUF wire

VTS died at the input queue with

  V4L2Device: (OUTPUT_MPLANE)VIDIOC_QBUF failed
  virtio-media: dmabuf covers 4096 bytes but the plane needs 2097152

The guard was right; the length was wrong. For V4L2_MEMORY_DMABUF the
plane length on the wire has to be the exporter's size, and only this
driver knows it when the descriptor chain is built. Userspace routinely
puts something else there: v4l2_codec2 fills every plane with the
queue's sizeimage because it skips QUERYBUF, while a decoder's input
block is a C2LinearBlock sized to the frame -- 28 bytes of SPS is one
page.

Import every plane and rewrite its length before the v4l2_buffer is
staged, then restore the caller's value on the way out. Both halves are
required:

 - The wire value must be EXACTLY the SG total. The device model
   concatenates the per-plane entry arrays and splits them apart by
   accumulating entry lengths until each plane's length is reached, so
   a short length would hand plane N's leftover entries to plane N+1,
   and a long one is rejected.
 - The caller's value must survive. @b is device-writable and the reply
   lands in it, and v4l2_codec2 reads that field back through
   getPlaneSize() as the queue's capacity -- leaving 4096 there would
   reject the NEXT, larger frame.

The rewrite has to precede scatterlist_builder_add_buffer(), which may
copy the buffer into the shadow buffer rather than map it by reference.
That is the same ordering constraint the DMABUF-to-USERPTR memory
substitution has, so the import moves next to it. The import is
idempotent (identity is the struct dma_buf *), so the one inside
scatterlist_builder_add_buffer_dmabuf() becomes a cache hit and its
coverage check stays live rather than becoming dead code.

Verified with an aarch64 guest running this driver against a
vivid-backed device model, before and after this change:

  before: FAIL QBUF(DMABUF, 4096-byte dmabuf, plane length 118784)
          -> -1 EINVAL
          dmesg: dmabuf covers 4096 bytes but the plane needs 118784
  after:  OK   QBUF ... -> 0
          OK   the caller's plane length survives: 118784

The other buffer tests pass before and after, and the decode tests fail
identically in both runs (vivid is not a decoder).

Change-Id: Ic5f1484b4de7a8118834f7527bb860e6d2ca68b9
Assisted-by: Claude Code:claude-opus-5
Signed-off-by: Yuichi Kusakabe <yuichi_kusakabe@jp.honda>
Upstream-Status: Pending
---
 driver/scatterlist_builder.c | 94 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 driver/scatterlist_builder.h |  4 ++
 driver/virtio_media_ioctls.c | 58 +++++++++++++++++++++-
 3 files changed, 154 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/driver/scatterlist_builder.c b/driver/scatterlist_builder.c
index 4f86898..d4c646d 100644
--- a/driver/scatterlist_builder.c
+++ b/driver/scatterlist_builder.c
@@ -567,6 +567,100 @@ static int virtio_media_import_dmabuf(struct scatterlist_builder *builder,
 	return 0;
 }
 
+/* Total number of bytes the entries of @sgt cover. */
+static size_t sgt_covered_bytes(struct sg_table *sgt)
+{
+	struct scatterlist *sg_iter;
+	size_t covered = 0;
+	int i;
+
+	for_each_sgtable_sg(sgt, sg_iter, i)
+		covered += sg_iter->length;
+
+	return covered;
+}
+
+/**
+ * scatterlist_builder_import_buffer_dmabuf() - Import every plane's dmabuf and
+ * make each plane length describe its exporter.
+ * @builder: builder to use. Its @dev must be set.
+ * @b: ``v4l2_buffer`` whose ``DMABUF`` planes are to be imported.
+ * @state: driver-side state of the buffer, which caches the imports.
+ *
+ * Why the plane length has to be rewritten, and why exactly to the SG total.
+ *
+ * For ``V4L2_MEMORY_DMABUF`` the plane length is the exporter's size, and only
+ * this driver knows it at the time the descriptor chain is built. Userspace
+ * routinely puts something else there: v4l2_codec2 fills every plane with the
+ * queue's ``sizeimage`` because it skips ``VIDIOC_QUERYBUF``, and its input
+ * (bitstream) blocks come from a C2LinearBlock sized to the frame -- a 28-byte
+ * SPS is one page. Measured on RPi4 2026-09-03, VTS ThumbnailTest:
+ *
+ *   V4L2Device: (OUTPUT_MPLANE)VIDIOC_QBUF failed
+ *   virtio-media: dmabuf covers 4096 bytes but the plane needs 2097152
+ *
+ * The guard was right and the length was wrong.
+ *
+ * The new length must be exactly the SG total, not a clamp of the caller's
+ * value: the device model concatenates every plane's entry array and splits it
+ * back apart by accumulating entry lengths until each plane's length is reached
+ * (virtio_media_qbuf() in hw/virtio/virtio-media.c). A length shorter than the
+ * bytes actually emitted for plane N would hand plane N's leftover entries to
+ * plane N+1. Larger is rejected outright by the same loop.
+ *
+ * Must run before scatterlist_builder_add_buffer(). That call may copy the
+ * v4l2_buffer and its plane array into the shadow buffer rather than mapping
+ * them by reference, so a later mutation would never reach the device. This is
+ * the same ordering constraint the DMABUF-to-USERPTR memory substitution has.
+ *
+ * The import itself is idempotent -- identity is the ``struct dma_buf *``, so
+ * the second import from scatterlist_builder_add_buffer_dmabuf() is a
+ * dma_buf_get()/compare/put() cache hit -- which is why that function is left
+ * unchanged and its coverage check stays live rather than becoming dead code.
+ *
+ * The caller is responsible for restoring the lengths userspace passed in; see
+ * virtio_media_send_buffer_ioctl().
+ */
+int scatterlist_builder_import_buffer_dmabuf(struct scatterlist_builder *builder,
+					     struct v4l2_buffer *b,
+					     struct virtio_media_buffer *state)
+{
+	int ret;
+	int i;
+
+	if (V4L2_TYPE_IS_MULTIPLANAR(b->type)) {
+		if (b->length > VIDEO_MAX_PLANES)
+			return -EINVAL;
+
+		for (i = 0; i < b->length; i++) {
+			struct v4l2_plane *plane = &b->m.planes[i];
+
+			if (plane->m.fd < 0)
+				return -EINVAL;
+
+			ret = virtio_media_import_dmabuf(
+				builder, &state->dmabufs[i], plane->m.fd);
+			if (ret)
+				return ret;
+
+			plane->length = (u32)sgt_covered_bytes(
+				state->dmabufs[i].sgt);
+		}
+	} else {
+		if (b->m.fd < 0)
+			return -EINVAL;
+
+		ret = virtio_media_import_dmabuf(builder, &state->dmabufs[0],
+						 b->m.fd);
+		if (ret)
+			return ret;
+
+		b->length = (u32)sgt_covered_bytes(state->dmabufs[0].sgt);
+	}
+
+	return 0;
+}
+
 /*
  * Emit one plane's virtio_media_sg_entry array from an already-mapped sg_table
  * into the shadow buffer, and reference it with a single descriptor.
diff --git a/driver/scatterlist_builder.h b/driver/scatterlist_builder.h
index 70cc855..c604be5 100644
--- a/driver/scatterlist_builder.h
+++ b/driver/scatterlist_builder.h
@@ -97,6 +97,10 @@ int scatterlist_builder_add_buffer(struct scatterlist_builder *builder,
 int scatterlist_builder_add_buffer_userptr(struct scatterlist_builder *builder,
 					   struct v4l2_buffer *b);
 
+int scatterlist_builder_import_buffer_dmabuf(struct scatterlist_builder *builder,
+					     struct v4l2_buffer *b,
+					     struct virtio_media_buffer *state);
+
 int scatterlist_builder_add_buffer_dmabuf(struct scatterlist_builder *builder,
 					  struct v4l2_buffer *b,
 					  struct virtio_media_buffer *state);
diff --git a/driver/virtio_media_ioctls.c b/driver/virtio_media_ioctls.c
index a70ce25..75b08a7 100644
--- a/driver/virtio_media_ioctls.c
+++ b/driver/virtio_media_ioctls.c
@@ -276,6 +276,8 @@ static int virtio_media_send_buffer_ioctl(struct v4l2_fh *fh, u32 ioctl,
 		.dev = vv->virtio_dev->dev.parent ?: &vv->virtio_dev->dev,
 	};
 	u32 orig_memory;
+	u32 orig_lengths[VIDEO_MAX_PLANES];
+	u32 num_planes = 0;
 	bool use_dmabuf;
 	size_t resp_len;
 	int ret;
@@ -319,6 +321,40 @@ static int virtio_media_send_buffer_ioctl(struct v4l2_fh *fh, u32 ioctl,
 		 * the device.
 		 */
 		b->memory = V4L2_MEMORY_USERPTR;
+
+		/*
+		 * The plane lengths go on the wire as the exporter's size,
+		 * and come back to userspace as it passed them.
+		 *
+		 * scatterlist_builder_import_buffer_dmabuf() explains why the
+		 * wire value has to be the SG total. It cannot simply be left
+		 * that way afterwards, because @b is mapped device-writable and
+		 * scatterlist_builder_retrieve_buffer() copies the host's reply
+		 * over the caller's plane array: userspace would get the
+		 * exporter's size back instead of what it set. v4l2_codec2
+		 * treats that field as the queue's capacity -- V4L2Decoder's
+		 * `request.buffer->size > getPlaneSize(0)` check -- so a
+		 * one-page input block would shrink the recorded capacity to
+		 * 4096 and the next larger frame would be rejected with
+		 * "The input size is not enough". Save and restore.
+		 */
+		if (V4L2_TYPE_IS_MULTIPLANAR(b->type)) {
+			if (b->length > VIDEO_MAX_PLANES) {
+				ret = -EINVAL;
+				goto restore_memory;
+			}
+			num_planes = b->length;
+			for (i = 0; i < num_planes; i++)
+				orig_lengths[i] = b->m.planes[i].length;
+		} else {
+			num_planes = 1;
+			orig_lengths[0] = b->length;
+		}
+
+		ret = scatterlist_builder_import_buffer_dmabuf(&builder, b,
+							      state);
+		if (ret)
+			goto restore_memory;
 	}
 
 	/* Command descriptor */
@@ -402,14 +438,32 @@ restore_memory:
 	 * can be answered. Fall back to @orig_memory when no buffers are
 	 * allocated, i.e. when there is no queue state to be authoritative.
 	 *
-	 * Plane lengths are deliberately left as the host wrote them --
-	 * scatterlist_builder_add_buffer_dmabuf()'s coverage check needs them.
+	 * On the USERPTR path the plane lengths are deliberately left as the
+	 * host wrote them -- scatterlist_builder_add_buffer()'s fixup and
+	 * scatterlist_builder_add_buffer_userptr() work off those. DMABUF is
+	 * the opposite case and is handled below.
 	 */
 	if (queue->allocated_bufs > 0)
 		b->memory = queue->memory;
 	else if (use_dmabuf)
 		b->memory = orig_memory;
 
+	/*
+	 * num_planes stays 0 when the goto fired before the lengths were
+	 * saved, and then there is nothing to put back.
+	 */
+	if (use_dmabuf && num_planes > 0) {
+		if (V4L2_TYPE_IS_MULTIPLANAR(b->type)) {
+			b->length = num_planes;
+			if (b->m.planes)
+				for (i = 0; i < num_planes; i++)
+					b->m.planes[i].length =
+						orig_lengths[i];
+		} else {
+			b->length = orig_lengths[0];
+		}
+	}
+
 	return ret;
 }
 
